        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Buy the tradable tabard or complete Shadowmourne's long quest chain and final chest turn-in.\n\n1. Choose the purchase or quest route. You can buy the actual Tabard of the Lightbringer (52252) on the Auction House or trade for it, then equip it directly; the buyer does not need Shadowmourne or a plate class. Compare the actual item rather than paying for an unrelated tabard or a promised chest drop. If purchasing, skip to step 14.\n\n2. For the quest route, use a Warrior, Paladin or Death Knight. Set Icecrown Citadel to 25-player and enter at 53.7, 87.0 in Icecrown. Kill entrance trash until Friendly with the Ashen Verdict, then accept The Sacred and the Corrupt from Highlord Darion Mograine on the left inside the entrance (42.6, 22.6 on The Lower Citadel map). Enable Trivial Quests if needed.\n\n3. With that quest active, go to Frostmourne Cavern in northeastern Dragonblight (74.4, 23.5). Interact with Light's Vengeance, wait through the Lich King's scene, use the hammer again as prompted and defeat the resurrected enemy. Collect the quest credit/item before leaving.\n\n4. Gather 25 Primordial Saronite and loot Rotface's Acidic Blood and Festergut's Acidic Blood from their 25-player kills. Return these and Light's Vengeance to Mograine's runeforge. Finish the forging turn-ins to receive Shadow's Edge.\n\n5. For A Feast of Souls, equip Shadow's Edge and collect 50 souls from Icecrown enemies. Apply Shadow's Fate BEFORE killing each target. At high level, use controlled or non-damaging abilities and watch the counter: Death Knights can apply it with Chains of Ice. Remove damage procs if enemies die before the debuff lands.\n\n6. Unholy Infusion: keep Shadow's Edge equipped and fight 25-player Professor Putricide. Bring a helper to hold his attention while you use the laboratory table to become an abomination. Let several slime pools form first; use Eat Ooze to absorb them until you have 100 energy, then cast Shadow Infusion. Once the infusion finishes and its buff is present, leave the vehicle and kill Putricide. Avoid procs or auto-attacks that kill him before the setup.\n\n7. Blood Infusion: bring three helpers to 25-player Blood-Queen Lana'thel and keep Shadow's Edge equipped. Stand beside the tank for Blood Mirror and arrange the initial vampire bite on the quest character. Personally bite three other players as Frenzied Bloodthirst enables Vampiric Bite. Coordinate helpers' own feeding, deaths or resurrection so your targets remain usable. Count all three personal bites before killing Lana'thel; quest credit is awarded after her death.\n\n8. Frost Infusion: with Shadow's Edge still equipped, face 25-player Sindragosa and survive FOUR Frost Breaths without dying. Hold damage, heal if necessary and remove retaliation/damage procs so she survives. After the frost infusion is applied, kill her and return to Mograine.\n\n9. Accept The Splintered Throne and collect 50 Shadowfrost Shards from eligible 25-player boss kills. This takes weekly lockouts; shards are not guaranteed from every boss. A second run on the same saved bosses or switching raid size does not supply another weekly set of drops.\n\n10. Finish forging Shadowmourne and accept The Lich King's Last Stand. With the completed legendary equipped and the relevant quest stage active, defeat the Lich King in 25-player Icecrown Citadel. Wait through the scripted death/resurrection and the final kill.\n\n11. Loot the Sealed Chest from that eligible kill BEFORE leaving or completing the remaining turn-ins. A random Lich King kill, or a repeat with an already completed legendary chain, does not create another chest.\n\n12. Return to Darion inside the entrance hall in that cleared raid. Complete Personal Property (24914) with the Sealed Chest, receive the Unsealed Chest and open it. Take the Badge of the Silver Hand from its contents.\n\n13. Speak to Uther the Lightbringer among the reward NPCs in the entrance hall of the instance where the Lich King has been defeated. Complete The Lightbringer's Redemption (24919) with the Badge for the tabard. Wait for each reward NPC's dialogue scene to finish before another turn-in. A fresh uncleared instance does not provide this reward scene.\n\n14. Equip the finished tabard to use its glow, or retain it unbound if intentionally trading it. A learned appearance can be transmogged on eligible alts, but the use effect requires the physical item. Keep it if you want the effect; transmogging another tabard to this appearance does not grant the glow.",
